1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Learn Marvelous Designer Tips in 3 Minutes

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Learn Marvelous Designer Tips in 3 Minutes

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
After a friend's question is saved,

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
the document cannot be opened again, and various prompt frames are removed.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
What is this about?

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
In fact, there are many reasons for such problems,

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
mainly related to the system font or the size of the document.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
When installing Marvelous Designer,

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
please make sure that there are no special fonts and non-English words in the installation path.

10
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
In other words, please try to avoid using special fonts such as signal, add, etc.,

11
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
and avoid Chinese, Japanese, Korean, etc.

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
In the same way, when storing project files or exporting files,

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000
please ensure that the path and file name are also in line with the above rules.

14
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Paths, such as this computer, local disk, etc. will not be affected.

15
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Just click on the specific path to comply with the previous rules.

16
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Recommend using Arabic, digital, English, and lowercase.

17
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
In addition, when using the internal function,

18
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
please try to ensure that you read the text,

19
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,000
and that the file path or name is in line with the above rules.

20
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Using special fonts or non-English words is not necessarily a problem,

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
but avoiding using them can avoid some unnecessary trouble.

22
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
In addition, it is sometimes impossible to open the files made in the new version

23
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
and open the files made in the new version in the old version.

24
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
However, it is possible to open the old version files in the new version software.

25
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
In addition, when the entire project file is larger than 2GB,

26
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
the files cannot be stored or may be damaged.

27
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The amount of clothing in the video is very small,

28
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,000
only 3mm, and the total number of animated frames is 1,500.

29
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Such project files are likely to be more than 2GB.

30
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
When we turn on the display statistics function,

31
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
at the bottom left corner of the 3D window,

32
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
you can see the number of faces, points, and other data.

33
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Next, let's test to save this file as a project file.

34
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Now go to the folder to check the file storage situation.

35
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
When we select this file,

36
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
you can see that the size of the entire file has become only more than 200KB,

37
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
which means that the storage has failed.

38
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
For such animated files that are more than 2GB,

39
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
it is best to record and save the project in a separate section at the beginning.

40
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
For example, here we recorded about 700 frames,

41
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
and then choose to save a project file.

42
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
After saving, the number of frames left at the beginning

43
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
stays at the last frame recorded just now,

44
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
and then delete the animation recorded before.

45
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
From the last frame just now,

46
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
continue to record the animation.

47
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
After recording a new animation,

48
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
continue to save as a new project file.

49
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
After saving in sections,

50
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:41,000
you can see that both project files have been successfully saved.

51
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
In addition, when the project is more than 2GB,

52
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
it can still be translated into Alembic format,

53
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
but it is not easy to modify in reverse,

54
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
so it is not recommended to directly export.

55
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
If you are not sure about the size of the entire project file,

56
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
you can first export the ABC file to check it.

57
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
The content of this issue ends here.

58
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,000
If you have any questions,

59
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
please send a private message or comment.

60
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
See you in the next video.

61
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Bye bye.

